WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.500
Your ring gear starts with a clear goal:

00:03.500 --> 00:07.000
finish-grind two opposing faces.

00:07.000 --> 00:12.000
Double-disc grinding removes material
from opposing part surfaces.

00:12.000 --> 00:18.000
The right approach depends on your geometry,
material, and finished-part requirements.

00:18.000 --> 00:22.500
Loading, unloading, and production needs
belong in the same conversation.

00:22.500 --> 00:28.000
C&B has published a ring-gear application
with robot loading and unloading.

00:28.000 --> 00:34.200
Share your material, part dimensions,
surface requirements, and production target.

00:34.200 --> 00:38.500
If details are still open,
mark them for discussion.

00:38.500 --> 00:43.000
You don't need to choose
a machine first.

00:43.000 --> 00:47.200
Bring the knowns and the questions together.

00:47.200 --> 00:51.000
Start a quote request with C&B Machinery,

00:51.000 --> 00:55.000
and build a clear brief for your
next engineering conversation.
